# S-044 quirk Q: output callbacks run under a recursive lock, in reverse registration order. A callback may disconnect
# itself (safe: every remaining input is still called once) or another input; removing an input with a LOWER index than
# the running one shifts the array under the reverse iteration, so the running input is called a second time.
aopen main 48000 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO
aconnect a 1 0
aconnect a 2 0
aconnect a 3 0
ahook a 3 disconnect_self
atick
adump
# removing an input that has not been visited yet (lower index) removes it from this pass too
aconnect a 3 0
ahook a 3 disconnect a 1
atick
adump
aclose
